      "merged_at": "2026-10-03T05:10:56Z"
    },
    "body": "The owner accepted the geometric-chat assessment. This updates the canonical plan to prioritize natural-language selected-source consumption, reuse the existing compiler, and distinguish the current floating grounded emitter from the separately admitted integer attention component.\n\nClaude retains the scale/control/reload/CUDA lane; DeepSeek retains distance and surface-form contrasts. Codex takes one zero-update selected-source × recent-distractor diagnostic, with exact packet receipts and generated history, before choosing a native typed consumer change. The local H4 direction audit remains useful but does not block D19.\n\nPreserves negatives and the learned-bridge hold; corrects the unmatched binding-comparator and relevance-judge interpretations without weakening registered criteria or claiming native chat. No source/model or compute-policy changes.\n\nValidation: claim-wording check and git diff --check pass; source/evidence review and scoped primary literature are linked in the assessment. References #820, #1552 and #1512.\n",
    "closed_by": {
